-# ShopEasy 2.8.86 — current release audit
-
-> **Status: QA candidate, not production-certified.** This release aligns deployment/setup documentation and active version labels with the existing Manager bootstrap implementation. It does not certify the full ecommerce application or change runtime authorization logic.
-
-## Integration test harness and release QA in 2.8.86
-
-- Fixed two static-audit tests that still attempted to scan the intentionally removed `api/` Vercel adapter directory. They now scan only the supported `src`, `public/js`, and `views` roots.
-- No production runtime behavior was changed by this test-harness patch. The four dependency-backed integration/template tests remain unverified in the authoring environment because npm registry access failed; they are not skipped or reported as passing.
-
-## Documentation/configuration alignment in 2.8.85
-
-- Confirmed that new deployment bootstrap uses `MANAGER_NAME`, `MANAGER_EMAIL` and `MANAGER_PASSWORD`; `ADMIN_EMAIL`/`ADMIN_PASSWORD` are mentioned only as legacy local-environment migration names, not as current bootstrap inputs.
-- Updated the staging runbook title, Manager bootstrap terminology, PowerShell password prompt, current deployment guide references, and stale active Manager/Staff/Settings version labels.
-- Added regression checks for these documentation/configuration contracts so future releases catch stale account terminology and current version labels.
-- No application authorization, rate-limit or database behavior is changed in this documentation-only release.
-
-## Decision
-
-Vercel/AWS Lambda serverless support is deliberately removed. Those hosts previously used a per-instance memory limiter that cannot be a shared security boundary, while production middleware fails closed with HTTP 503 when shared protection is unavailable. Rather than introduce a database write for every limited request (which would contend with orders and consume the same free database quota), this candidate supports only a single persistent Node.js instance using `RATE_LIMIT_BACKEND=memory-single-instance` until a shared limiter is implemented. Cloudflare Worker deployment is now blocked because the production runtime rejects PBKDF2 iterations above 100,000, below ShopEasy’s 600,000 requirement. Vercel builds fail explicitly and the Vercel API adapter is removed.
-
-## Retained runtime behavior from 2.8.84
-
-- Database module fails clearly if Vercel/AWS Lambda serverless environment variables are detected.
-- `vercel.json` calls `scripts/reject-vercel-deploy.mjs`, which exits non-zero with a clear deployment-target message instead of building a misleading static-only site.
-- `src/server.js`, image storage path, session maintenance and proxy defaults no longer claim Vercel support. Local Node development remains available; persistent single-process Node production must explicitly configure `RATE_LIMIT_BACKEND=memory-single-instance`.
-- `scripts/create-staff.mjs` uses `SHOP_DATABASE_URL` for an explicitly confirmed remote Turso target rather than pretending Vercel is its adapter.
-- Manager integration harness no longer sets `VERCEL=1`; temporary BLOB image storage is enabled only under `NODE_ENV=test`.
-- QA tests, release preflight and deployment documentation were updated.
-
-## Free-tier database/hosting limitation
-
-Turso Free currently lists 5 GB storage, 500 million rows read/month and 10 million rows written/month. Cloudflare Workers Free lists 100,000 requests/day and 10 ms CPU/request; Durable Objects Free lists 100,000 requests/day. The current app stores uploaded-image BLOBs in Turso and reserves up to 2 GiB for them, so order rows, indexes, sessions, audit logs and other business data share the remaining database space. These figures are published quotas, not a guarantee of simultaneous users or orders/day. There is no unlimited free tier.
-
-The PBKDF2 work factor remains 600,000 iterations and must not be weakened to fit a free CPU limit. Production Cloudflare Workers also rejects a single PBKDF2 deriveBits call above 100,000 iterations; local `wrangler dev` does not reliably expose this cap. Cloudflare deploy/dry-run commands now fail closed. Benchmark login, registration and password reset on the actual persistent Node.js staging host before production.
-
-## Verification status
-
-The checked-in tests, syntax checks, static audit, template audit, Cloudflare build, and live staging checks must all be run on a complete dependency installation. A source-level pass or a missing-dependency skip is not a pass. Current report: [FIX6 QA report](docs/qa/AUDIT-R22-FIX6-WINDOWS-TEST-REPAIRS-2026-11-08.md).
