+# Features and limitations — R27 / 2.8.94
+
+“Included” below means implemented in the inspected source. It does not mean every role, edge case, language, device, external provider or production host has been tested. Use fresh release verification and buyer QA outputs tied to the delivered ZIP/source hashes; older reports are historical evidence.
+
+| Area | Included capability | Practical limit / buyer verification |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Catalogue | Categories, nested filtering, products, tags/search, sorting/pagination, scheduled sales, stories, gallery and archive/restore. | Seller content/images need rights and quality review. Category write validation is transactional and recursive queries terminate with `UNION`; remote DB behavior still needs testing. |
+| Product options | Up to 50 option rows, with one or two option dimensions such as colour × size; row stock/SKU/image; gallery association. | Not an arbitrary N-dimensional configurator. Removed ordered combinations are retained inactive for history. Reserved stock cannot be silently removed. |
+| Pricing | Currency-aware integer minor units, per-product automatic discounts, coupons and optional bundle rules; SQL/display sale timestamp normalization. | One store currency. Before first order, currency precision rescaling is not foreign-exchange conversion and requires price review. Historical amounts are not converted. |
+| Inventory | Transactional checkout reservations, restock controls, low-stock dashboard and protected lifecycle changes. | Pending reservations have no automatic expiry. No warehouse/carrier integration or automatic low-stock email; opt-in customer stock alerts are separate. |
+| Checkout | Server validation of current stock, price, delivery/tax rules, terms and session intent; guest and account purchases; COD default. | Launch fields must be configured for the actual market. A launch checklist is not legal/tax certification. |
+| Bank transfer | Pending orders with saved instructions; Manager verifies statement and confirms exact amount, currency and unique reference. | Manual reconciliation; no bank API, statement import or automatic receipt verification. |
+| Card payments | Mollie payment creation, provider-hosted checkout, server API reconciliation/webhook validation and financial snapshots. | Only integrated card transaction adapter. Merchant country/currency, credentials, HTTPS and environment gates apply. Live/sandbox settlement, refunds and provider account eligibility require buyer tests. No PAN/CVV collection by ShopEasy. |
+| Provider directory | Official onboarding/contact entries and private representative notes. | PayTabs, FIB, iyzico, ZainCash and Stripe are directory entries, not implemented checkout adapters. |
+| Gift cards | Manager issuance, hashed codes, balance/ledger, full-cover checkout and internal credit/refund controls. | Gift card must cover the full order; no split tender. External cash/card refunds are not executed by the returns tool. Financial records remain subject to operator retention. |
+| Orders | Customer history, order status history, supported cancellation/request flow, Manager fulfilment and payment reconciliation. | Registered orders require their owner; guest orders require the bearer via protected cookie or explicit private-code POST. Email/order number alone grants no access. Lost guest access needs identity-checked support. |
+| Returns/exchanges | Request, approval/rejection, arrival/inspection/restock, refund recording and exchange tracking reference. | Refund recording requires money already sent via the real method; no bank/provider refund transfer or courier tracking API. |
+| Delivery/tax | Country allow-list, flat fee and optional country/city/postal-prefix fee and percentage-tax rules; accepted policy snapshots. | Operator-entered arithmetic, not statutory-rate discovery, exemptions/thresholds, multi-tax engine, registrations, filings or compliance. |
+| Customer account | Signup/login/logout, password change, configurable email verification and reset. | New/set/reset passwords use 15 Unicode characters plus a small offline example/repetition blocklist; no complete breached-password database. Existing login verification is preserved. Email flows require actual sender/inbox validation. |
+| Staff | Full Manager role, TOTP/recovery codes, restricted overview-only Admin, staff/account management and audit events. | Not configurable fine-grained staff RBAC. A complete role/action/error matrix and deployment access review remain buyer work. |
+| Engagement | Newsletter confirmation/unsubscribe/campaign batches, confirmed stock alerts and verified-purchase reviews with moderation. | Delivery depends on email configuration/provider. No marketing deliverability or consent-law certification. |
+| Email | Resend-based verification/reset, optional order confirmation/status and engagement emails, claims/caps for supported flows. | Order messages default off. No carrier tracking or general Manager order-notification service. Intercepted QA email is SIMULATED; no proof of inbox delivery. |
+| AI | Optional bounded search phrase expansion and shopping-assistant responses using up to 12 public catalogue entries; catalogue search results come from real active stored products; private server key and production HTTPS endpoint allowlist. | Model instructions restrict invented claims but do not guarantee answer accuracy. AI has no stock/price authority. External requests/costs, output quality and privacy need operator review. Pattern-based redaction cannot guarantee all identifiers are removed. |
+| E-invoicing | Manager form and configured Recommand/Peppol transport with submission tracking/idempotency. | Actual network acceptance/recipient delivery and invoice-law/tax correctness require market/provider testing. Not a complete accounting system. |
+| Language/UI | English, Sorani Kurdish, Arabic, Dutch and French interface, RTL layouts, server-translated selected pages, seller-text preservation in quick preview, keyboard/accessibility corrections. | Product/category/story text is seller-authored. Policy/branding fields need reviewed translations; fallback is disclosed. Every translation and screen-reader/device state is not verified. No full WCAG 2.2 AA certification. |
+| SEO | Canonicals/hreflang, sitemap/robots controls, product/organization structured data and private-page noindex. | Real domain/search-console/indexing behavior and field accuracy depend on operator setup. No ranking or production Core Web Vitals guarantee. |
+| Privacy | Manager data export, eligible deletion and explicit contact minimization retaining financial records with policy reference/acknowledgement. | Retained financial references/ledger and country/dates/amounts can remain linkable: pseudonymity, not legal erasure/anonymity. Policies, backups, processors, legal holds and off-app records remain operator responsibility. |
+| Backups | Streamed compressed AES-256-GCM logical DB/media backup, checksum, separate-empty-target restore with checks. | Manual/on-demand; no hosted schedule, automatic off-site upload, key custody or guaranteed recovery. Rehearse host recovery. |
+| Deployment | Persistent Linux Node/Caddy/systemd path, staged release preparation, atomic code-pointer switch, health/readiness and code rollback attempt; cross-platform production-start wrapper. | Restart may cause downtime. Code rollback does not undo migrations/data. Windows/macOS operation and real host rollback are not established by Linux checks. |
+| Other targets | libSQL/Turso configuration and Cloudflare build/DO source retained. | Cloudflare auth/deploy gate stays closed for the PBKDF2 runtime incompatibility. Vercel/AWS Lambda and multi-instance memory limiting unsupported. |
+| QA | Isolated Node workers; Python 3.13 / Playwright 1.62.0 synthetic fixture; local customer/TOTP/COD/ownership flows; optional axe and no-JS/CSP checks. | Route/assertion totals are not exhaustive journeys. Axe incomplete items need manual disposition. Synthetic email, persisted-pageshow simulation and local provider doubles must stay labelled. |
+
+## Verification and legal boundaries
+
+The shipped [QA guide](qa/README.md), [Staging runbook](STAGING-QA-RUNBOOK.md) and [Release verification](RELEASE-VERIFICATION.md) explain how to collect fresh evidence. Full manual source/translation review, requirement-by-requirement ASVS, an exhaustive penetration test, all WCAG success criteria, real assistive technology/physical devices, real provider delivery/settlement/acceptance, production load and Windows PowerShell 5.1 execution remain unestablished by these documents. No “100% safe”, “fully compliant” or “ready to sell” claim follows from a successful command.
+
+Dependency notices cover 105 locked `node_modules` rows: 104 external entries and one first-party local alias. The replacement `@shopeasy/task-limit` stays private/UNLICENSED with effective rights UNKNOWN. npm advisory inventories can count 106 components by also counting the local vendor workspace. Read [Third-party notices](THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md), including all **nine OPEN native embedded-component review gates**; successful notice collection is not a native/legal clearance.
+
+The seller has confirmed no documentary source/asset ownership evidence. Effective ownership, assignments, asset licences and final buyer grant remain UNKNOWN. [Buyer use intent](SELLER-PROTECTION-PACK/BUYER-USE-INTENT.md) records editing/rebranding intent only. [The rights register](RIGHTS-CLEARANCE-REGISTER.md), draft [license](LICENSE.txt), [asset register](ASSET-PROVENANCE-REGISTER.md) and [Seller Protection Pack](SELLER-PROTECTION-PACK/README.md) must be completed with evidence and authorized acceptance. Do not turn an unresolved register into a clearance by changing its wording.
