-Manager → Settings → **Choose one currency for this store**. Select the single currency the whole store will use; the list includes EUR, IQD, SYP, USD and other supported currencies. Language, delivery country and currency are separate settings. Choosing Arabic does not automatically select IQD or SYP, and ShopEasy does not convert currencies using exchange rates.
+Before the first order, changing currency adjusts product prices/costs/sales, fixed coupons and monetary coupon minimums to the new minor-unit precision in one transaction. For example, a numerical value of 89 is precision-rescaled, not converted to the target currency's market value. Delivery fee resets to zero. Set correct target-market amounts and confirm the separate price-review control before checkout reopens. After the first order exists, the store currency is locked to its historical order currency; a mismatched change is blocked. Existing orders are never converted and aggregate reports assume one currency.
 
-You can save Settings before adding products or buying stock. The Launch Check determines whether checkout may accept orders; it does not prevent saving configuration drafts. If products or money-based coupons exist, changing currency is allowed before the first order. ShopEasy adjusts prices, costs, sale prices, fixed coupon values and monetary coupon minimums transactionally to the new currency's supported decimal precision; it does not apply an exchange rate (for example EUR 89.00 is scaled to IQD 89.000 for storage precision only, not the current market-equivalent IQD amount). Delivery fee resets to zero. Checkout stays closed until every affected amount is set to the actual target-market price and the price review is confirmed. After any order exists, currency changes are locked because current dashboard/customer/profit totals assume one currency. Do not interpret precision-rescaled numbers as market prices.
+## Configure delivery and tax rules
 
-## Set the delivery charge
+Enter only **Countries where you actually deliver**. The server rejects checkout destinations outside that allow-list. Set the default **Delivery fee per order** (`0` for free delivery), charged once per order in the store currency.
 
-Manager → Settings → **Delivery fee per order**. This fee is added once to the full order, not for each product. Enter `0` for free delivery. It uses the selected store currency. This version supports one flat delivery fee; it does not yet support country/region-specific shipping zones, carrier rates, or automatic country-specific tax calculation.
-
-## Policy text per language
-
-Manager → Settings → **Provide policy text per language**. English policy texts are required for the basic launch gate. Dutch, Sorani and Arabic are separate optional translation fields. A blank translation displays a notice before/when the English version is shown; it is not automatically translated. Get market-appropriate privacy, terms, delivery and return wording reviewed before using the store commercially. Orders record the terms locale, acceptance timestamp and hash of the policy text that was accepted.
-
-## Customer cancellation flow
-
-- `Pending`: the customer can cancel; the system attempts a single transactional status transition and releases reserved inventory once.
-- `Processing`: the customer can submit a reasoned cancellation request. It is not cancelled until a manager accepts the request.
-- `Shipped`: normal cancellation is no longer offered in the customer UI; use the store's contact/return process.
-- `Completed`: treat a problem as a return/refund workflow rather than a pre-delivery cancellation.
-
-Test this with a disposable staging product/order before using real customer orders. Guest customers need the original browser's protected order-access cookie to use the guest cancellation form.
-
-## Add a product
-Manager → Products → Add product. Fill in name, SKU, category, regular price and add an image. For a simple product with no options (for example, flowers), leave **This product has options** unchecked and enter one stock quantity. For a product with one option type (for example, shoes with sizes), check **This product has options** and enter an option name such as `Size`. The editor now gives you separate rows for each option: enter `42` with its stock, click **+ Add another option**, then add `43`, `44`, `45`, etc. You can remove rows, use the quick size presets, and see the total stock update as you type. You can add up to 50 unique options. The customer must choose an in-stock option; stock is tracked separately for each option. Only one option type per product is supported in this version (not size *and* colour combinations). Existing ordered option values are kept in order history.
-
-### Add a product discount
-Inside the same product form, use **Sale price** for a scheduled sale and **Automatic discount %** for an additional per-product discount. Optionally set **Sale starts** and **Sale ends**. Save. The storefront shows the final lower price when the rules are active.
-
-### Add a coupon
-Manager → Discounts → Create coupon. Choose Percentage or Fixed amount, set the value, optional minimum order and optional expiry, then activate it.
-
-### Add a story
-Manager → Stories → Create story. Add title, text, image, publication date, expiry date and optionally attach a product.
-
-### Manage an order
-Manager → Orders → open an order. The manager can see:
-- customer email
-- customer phone
-- customer name
-- full delivery address
-- city/postal code/country
-- customer note
-- purchased items
-- verified server-side total
-- payment reference when available
-Then move the order through the allowed fulfilment states.
-
-### AI
-Manager → Settings → Optional AI. Only the Manager role can change global store settings; the Admin role cannot access this page.
-The switch controls the feature only when the server-side AI provider is configured. The API key is never shown in the browser. To remove AI completely, delete `src/services/ai.js` and remove the `AI_*` environment variables.
-
-
-## Staff accounts
-
-ShopEasy 2.8.93 includes a Manager-only **Staff & account** screen at `/admin/staff`. Use it to create restricted Admin accounts, remove an Admin after confirming the current Manager password, and change the Manager login email/password. `.env` bootstraps only the first Manager; it never creates Admins or resets an existing Manager. Never make a customer an Admin by editing database roles manually.
-
-## Per-product automatic discount
-In **Products → Edit**, set **Automatic discount %** from 0–90%. This percentage applies **only to that product**, for every customer. Set it to **0%** to disable it. The server recalculates it at checkout and records the automatic discount separately from any coupon discount.
-
-The launch gate also checks the business phone and enterprise/registration number before live checkout is allowed.
-
-## Configure delivery coverage before accepting orders
-
-In **Manager → Settings → Currency & Delivery**, enter one country per line in **Countries where you actually deliver**. Only countries you can reliably deliver to and collect cash in should be listed. The checkout offers these countries and the server rejects any country outside the configured list. This is a country-level allow-list only; it does not configure delivery by city, province, postcode, carrier or remote area. Confirm the actual coverage and fee before enabling orders.
-
-### Add more stock to an existing product
-Open **Products → Edit** for the exact product. Use the separate **Quick restock / Add stock** box and enter only the number of units arriving. Do not use the main **Save product** form just to add stock. The restock action changes quantity only; it does not require you to re-enter the sale price or purchase cost, and it does not rewrite the SKU, stored prices, image or completed order history. If the product has options, restock the specific option row.
-
-### Understand price fields and validation
-- **Regular price** is the normal price paid for one unit before discounts.
-- **Purchase cost per unit** is what the shop paid for one unit. It is private manager information used for the gross-profit estimate.
-- **Sale price** is optional. Leave it blank if there is no sale; if entered, it must be greater than zero and lower than the regular price.
-- **Automatic discount %** is a separate optional discount that applies only to this product. `0` means off. Do not enter the discounted customer total into the automatic-discount field.
-
-The price input accepts comma decimals (for example `32,80`) and point decimals (`32.80`) in the selected store currency. Thousands separators are also accepted when correctly grouped. ShopEasy does not convert between currencies. If the form reports a sale-price error, check that Sale price is below Regular price or leave it blank when only using an automatic percentage discount.
-
-### Set how long a new order holds stock
-Pending orders have no automatic time limit. They remain visible until a manager accepts, declines or cancels them; reserved stock remains held while the order is pending. The order list shows a relative age (for example, 1 hour ago, 1 day ago or 17 days ago), and the exact date/time is available on hover.
-
-### Read the cart and coupon totals
-The cart shows the subtotal at regular item prices, automatic product discounts, coupon discount, delivery and the final cash-on-delivery total as separate lines. When a product has an automatic discount, its unit price before and after that discount is shown. The coupon amount is calculated after eligible automatic product discounts. Use **Continue shopping** to go back to the catalog without losing the current bag.
-
-
-## Product archive, restore and permanent deletion
-
-1. Open **Manage → Products** and choose **Product status** to view all, live or archived products.
-2. **Archive** hides the product from customers but preserves its product record and historical order references. A product with reserved checkout stock cannot be archived until the active order is completed or cancelled.
-3. To bring it back, select **Archived products** and press **Restore**. The product becomes visible again, but it is not automatically featured on the homepage.
-4. **Delete permanently** is available only for an archived product that has no order-item history and no reserved stock. When a product has appeared in any order, the interface tells you to keep it archived. This is intentional and protects historical records.
-
-
-## Saving drafts and changing store currency (2.8.64)
-
-The Launch Check controls whether checkout can accept orders; it must not block saving business details, currency, delivery setup or policy drafts. You can save with zero products and zero delivery countries, then add stock later when the budget permits.
-
-You can change the store currency after adding products or monetary coupons, provided the store has no order history yet. On a currency change, product regular prices, purchase costs, sale prices, fixed coupon values and monetary coupon minimums are adjusted to the target currency's minor-unit precision in one transaction. This is **not an exchange-rate conversion**: EUR 89.00 is scaled to IQD 89.000 for storage precision only, not the market-equivalent Iraqi dinar value. The delivery fee resets to zero. Checkout is paused until the manager enters real target-market prices, checks every affected product/coupon value, and confirms the separate price-review checkbox on Settings.
-
-After the first order exists, the store currency is locked. Current dashboard, customer lifetime-value and profit summaries assume one currency; allowing a second currency without currency-grouped reporting could make financial totals misleading. If a shop that has order history must operate in another currency, use a separate store/database or implement and verify multi-currency reporting before changing the currency.
-
-
-## Regional delivery and tax settings (2.8.93)
-
-Open **Manage → Settings → Currency & delivery**. The country list is the outer allow-list. Optional delivery overrides use one rule per line in this format:
+Optional regional delivery overrides use one rule per line:
 
 ```text
 Country | City or * | Postal prefix or * | Fee
@@ -139,22 +42,91 @@
 Country | City or * | Postal prefix or * | Rate % | Tax shipping (yes/no)
 ```
 
-A more-specific city/postal-prefix rule takes precedence. When tax rules are configured, a checkout destination without a matching rule is blocked; do not rely on a guessed 0% rate. The seller must verify every rate and shipping-tax treatment before enabling checkout. These settings are arithmetic rules only: ShopEasy does not look up statutory rates, implement product exemptions or thresholds, calculate multiple tax layers, determine registrations, file returns or certify legal compliance. Do not market them as a complete international tax engine.
+More-specific city/postal-prefix rules take precedence. When tax rules exist, a destination without a match is blocked. Verify the actual coverage, fee, rate and shipping-tax treatment. These are operator-entered arithmetic rules: no carrier rates/booking/tracking, statutory-rate lookup, product exemptions, thresholds, multiple tax layers, registrations or filings are implemented.
 
-## Returns, exchanges and refunds (2.8.93)
+## Enter policy text per language
 
-Open **Returns** in the Manager navigation to review requests. Approve or reject each request, record the item arrival, optionally restock only after inspection, and record a refund only after money was actually sent via the real payment method. ShopEasy does not transfer refunds or contact a bank. For exchanges, record the replacement shipment/tracking reference and close only after delivery is confirmed. All actions are manager-only and CSRF-protected.
+**Settings → Policy text** has separate English, Sorani Kurdish, Arabic, Dutch and French fields. The basic launch gate requires English policies; missing translations show a notice that English is displayed. Policies are not machine-translated. Have applicable privacy, terms, delivery and return text reviewed for the actual market. Orders snapshot accepted terms locale, timestamp and hash. Policy templates do not establish consent-law, consumer-law or privacy compliance.
 
-## Low stock and data recovery
+## Add products, option combinations and images
 
-The dashboard counts active products/variants where available stock is at or below the configured reorder threshold. It does not send email alerts. For encrypted DB + image backups, snapshot restore, checksum and recovery rehearsal, follow `DATABASE-BACKUP-RESTORE.md`. Test restores only into a separate empty database; never overwrite the live customer database.
+Open **Products → Add product**. Enter name, SKU, category, regular price, purchase cost and image. For a simple product, leave **This product has options** off and enter its stock. For options, enable it and set one or two option names, such as `Colour` and `Size`. Add a row for each sellable combination (`Blue / M`, `Blue / L`, etc.), with its own stock, SKU and optional image. One-dimensional options remain supported. Up to **50 unique combination rows** are accepted; this is not an arbitrary multi-dimensional configurator.
 
-## Payment methods and bank contacts
+Add gallery images and associate a row with the appropriate image. Customers must select an available combination; stock is revalidated server-side. Existing ordered option snapshots remain in order history. Removing a combination makes the stored row inactive; reserved combinations cannot be removed or have stock reduced below reservations. Use clear seller-written names/descriptions and review all language needs yourself.
 
-Open **Manage → Settings → Payment methods and provider setup**. Cash on delivery is the default. Choose **Cash on delivery only** until a card provider has approved your real legal business and payout account. **Cash on delivery + card** never forces customers to pay by card; card appears only when the supported integration passes all eligibility and environment checks.
+Price fields:
 
-Only Mollie hosted card checkout is integrated in this build. Store API keys in the server environment, never in this form. Production card payments require `NODE_ENV=production`, the public HTTPS `BASE_URL`, and a Mollie live key in `MOLLIE_API_KEY`. A dedicated non-production staging site may use a test key only when `MOLLIE_TEST_CHECKOUT_ENABLED=true`. Never test with real card transactions until provider onboarding and your pricing/refund practices are approved.
+- **Regular price** is the per-unit price before discounts.
+- **Purchase cost per unit** is private Manager input for a gross-profit estimate; it is not full accounting profit.
+- **Sale price** is optional, greater than zero and below regular price; optional start/end dates schedule it.
+- **Automatic discount %** (0–90%) applies to that product; `0` disables it. The server calculates it separately from coupon discounts.
 
-The provider directory contains official contact and onboarding pages. FIB's official site lists `customer_care@fib.iq` and 6977 within Iraq; iyzico's official contact page lists +90 216 599 01 00. Contact details entered under **Private Manager Notes** are internal-only reminders for your own representative and are not shown to customers. Do not store bank passwords, account login credentials, card numbers, CVV or API keys there. PayTabs, FIB, iyzico, ZainCash and Stripe are directory-only in this version; their transactions must not be offered as active checkout methods.
+Comma/point decimals and correctly grouped thousands separators are accepted according to the selected currency's precision; there is no exchange-rate conversion. Check scheduled dates in the configured time zone. SQL catalogue filters/sorts and displayed sale prices use consistent timestamp interpretation.
 
-If your business is in Syria or has Syrian legal/settlement links, check restrictions directly with the provider and qualified compliance support. Mollie's published merchant-country list excludes Syria and Stripe prohibits direct or indirect dealings linked to Syria. Do not select another country just to pass the form; use COD until you have documented eligibility for a provider and payout account.
+## Restock and read inventory
+
+Use **Products → Edit → Quick restock / Add stock** for arriving quantities. Enter the **additional** units only; for option products choose the exact row. This changes quantity without rewriting SKU, price, cost, image or order history. The main product form edits the intended stock level and protects reserved stock.
+
+The dashboard counts active products/combinations where available stock is at/below the reorder threshold. It does not email the Manager a low-stock alert. Optional opt-in customer restock emails are separate and require actual email configuration/testing.
+
+## Archive, restore and delete products
+
+Use the **Product status** filter for live/archived items. **Archive** hides a product while retaining history; it refuses active reserved stock. **Restore** republishes an archived product without automatically featuring it. **Delete permanently** is allowed for an active or archived product with no order-item history and no reserved stock. Keep historically ordered products archived rather than deleting financial/support references.
+
+## Discounts, bundles and stories
+
+**Discounts** creates percentage/fixed coupons, optional minimum subtotal and expiry. Product automatic discounts are shown separately in the cart; coupon calculations use the eligible discounted subtotal. Optional **Bundles** rules apply the configured combination discount. Review real cart/checkout totals before enabling any promotion.
+
+**Stories → Create story** accepts title, text, image, publication/expiry dates and optional product/link. Story text is seller-authored. Use only permitted content and verify dates/visibility in the storefront.
+
+## Choose payment methods
+
+**Settings → Payment methods and provider setup** defaults to COD. Enable methods the actual business can operate.
+
+- **Manual bank transfer** saves instructions with the order. Verify the actual bank statement, exact amount/currency and unique transaction reference before using **Confirm bank transfer**. There is no bank API or automatic receipt check.
+- **Mollie hosted card checkout** is the implemented card adapter. It needs merchant-country/currency eligibility, private `MOLLIE_API_KEY`, public HTTPS `BASE_URL` and environment gates. Production requires `NODE_ENV=production`, a live key and `MOLLIE_LIVE_CHECKOUT_APPROVED=true`. A dedicated non-production staging host permits a test key only with `MOLLIE_TEST_CHECKOUT_ENABLED=true`. The provider hosts card entry; ShopEasy does not store PAN/CVV. Server API verification binds payment to the order/reference/amount/currency/mode; a browser success page is not payment proof.
+- PayTabs, FIB, iyzico, ZainCash and Stripe are **directory/onboarding entries**, not implemented transaction methods. Private representative notes must not contain API keys, bank passwords or card details.
+
+Check eligibility/KYC/payout restrictions with the actual provider using the correct legal country. Do not enter a false country to pass a form. Built-in adapter support does not prove live settlement, refund behavior or onboarding; validate these using controlled staging/provider accounts. Configure keys in the private server environment, never a browser field.
+
+## Manage orders and held stock
+
+**Orders → Open order** shows customer/contact/destination data, item snapshots, verified totals, payment/reference data, notes and status history. Protect this personal information. COD normally moves **pending → processing → shipped → completed**. Completion means cash was actually collected/delivery completed; it consumes stock and records the cash-received reference. Verified card/bank/gift-card payments use **paid → processing → shipped → completed**. Use only actions currently allowed by the server.
+
+New pending orders have **no automatic reservation timeout**. Reserved stock remains held through active fulfilment; completion consumes it, and supported cancellation releases it once. A paid marker alone does not remove physical on-hand stock. Check stale pending orders manually. The order list shows age with exact time available; it is not an expiry countdown.
+
+For a Mollie attempt with an uncertain/missing local reference, reconcile the exact payment ID from the provider dashboard. ShopEasy fetches/validates it; entering an ID alone does not mark the order paid. **Refresh financial status** records provider-reported refunded/charged-back totals and does not send money. Legacy pending orders can be confirmed as COD only through the guarded action when no online-payment details exist and stock reservations are intact.
+
+## Customer access and cancellation
+
+Registered order access requires the authenticated owner. Guest lookup/actions require the valid bearer through the protected HttpOnly cookie or explicit private-code POST field; email plus order number is insufficient and URL bearers are rejected. Lost guest access needs the operator's identity-checked support process.
+
+- Pending COD customers can cancel through the supported form; inventory is released once transactionally.
+- Processing COD customers can submit a reasoned cancellation request; cancellation waits for Manager acceptance.
+- Pending bank-transfer cancellation is request-only so the Manager can check actual receipt first.
+- Paid card/bank/gift-card orders do not offer a general pre-shipment provider refund workflow; resolve payment and customer support before any permitted action.
+- Shipped/completed orders use contact/returns handling instead of ordinary pre-delivery cancellation.
+
+Do not force a rejected action with manual database edits. Refresh the order, reconcile payment/reservations and record what actually happened.
+
+## Returns, exchanges and refunds
+
+Open **Returns** to approve/reject a request, record arrival, inspect and optionally restock. Record a refund only after money was sent using the real method; record exchange shipment/reference and close after confirmed delivery. The return tool records events; it does not contact a bank, execute a Mollie refund or book/track a courier. Gift-card credit is a separate internal ledger action. Verify exact quantities/amounts and avoid duplicate external/internal refunds.
+
+## Gift cards, customer engagement and invoices
+
+**Gift cards** can enable the feature, issue a currency-bound card and inspect balances/ledger. Keep a new code private; stored codes are hashed. A gift card must cover the complete order; split tender is not implemented. Use the guarded credit/refund action with actual order context.
+
+**Reviews** moderates verified-purchase reviews. **Newsletter** creates campaigns and sends bounded batches to eligible confirmed subscribers. Stock alerts also require confirmation. Check consent/retention and actual email delivery. Order-confirmation/status email is separately opt-in and off by default; there is no general carrier-tracking or Manager order-notification integration.
+
+**E-invoicing** provides the configured Recommand/Peppol submission path and tracking; recipient acceptance and legal/tax correctness must be verified for the actual market. A generated record/PDF is not proof of structured-invoice delivery or full accounting compliance.
+
+## Optional AI
+
+**Settings → Optional AI** controls the feature when a private server-side endpoint/key/model are configured. The key is never shown in the browser. AI expands bounded search phrases and can answer shopping questions using up to 12 public catalogue entries. Search results still come from active real products; AI cannot set authoritative price/stock, and model instructions do not guarantee answer accuracy. Disable the setting/environment flag to turn it off; follow [AI integration](AI-INTEGRATION.md) when changing/removing the module. Review external data/costs and provider configuration; pattern redaction is not a guarantee that every identifier is removed.
+
+## Privacy, audits and recovery
+
+Use **GDPR** only after verifying the requester and reviewing the operator's documented retention/legal-hold policy. Choose export, eligible deletion or explicit financial-record minimization. Minimization requires the policy reference and acknowledgement and retains financial references/ledger; it is pseudonymous retained data, not certified legal erasure/anonymity. Read the complete [privacy procedure in the Admin guide](ADMIN-GUIDE.md#5-use-privacy-actions-under-a-documented-policy) before acting. Account roles, backups and records held by outside services require separate processes.
+
+**Audit** shows application events; protect logs and investigate failed or inconsistent changes before retrying. [Backup and restore](DATABASE-BACKUP-RESTORE.md) covers encrypted DB/media backups and restore into a separate empty target. Secure keys separately and rehearse recovery. [Deployment](DEPLOYMENT.md) code rollback does not restore database state. Actual host/provider delivery/settlement, Windows/macOS and complete accessibility/security coverage remain separate validation work described in [Features and limitations](FEATURES-AND-LIMITATIONS.md).
