-## Features and historical development notes (R12.11–R22)
-
-ShopEasy is a reusable online-store starter for retail businesses. It includes product and category management, stock and product options, coupons, stories, customer accounts, cash-on-delivery orders, customer cancellation requests, a full-access Manager role and a restricted overview-only Admin role, audit events, English/Sorani/Arabic/Dutch/French UI, and local Node.js development and a persistent single-instance Node.js production path. Cloudflare Workers is an optional alternative and its current deployment workflow remains blocked until the 600,000-iteration PBKDF2 flow is proven compatible there; the Oracle persistent Node.js + local SQLite route is documented in DEPLOYMENT.md. Vercel/AWS Lambda serverless deployment is deliberately rejected.
-
-REPAIR13 adds a **manual bank-transfer** option (Manager verifies actual bank receipt and confirms the exact amount/reference; no automatic bank API) and optional AI-assisted catalog search (AI proposes bounded query expansions; ShopEasy returns only real active products from its own database). Mollie-hosted checkout remains the only implemented card-provider transaction adapter. Provider names such as FIB, PayTabs, iyzico, ZainCash and Stripe are contact/onboarding references, not integrations. These paths are QA candidates and still require staging validation.
-
-Older design/security/payment reports were omitted from this clean handover; retain the full FIX6 developer archive if historic evidence is needed. Open [the E2 storefront preview](PREVIEW.html) and [the E2 Manager preview](PREVIEW-MANAGER.html) to inspect the refreshed visual system. Both pages use sample content only and do not process orders.
-
-This is a **starter and QA candidate**, not a universal commerce platform or a certification. The default configuration is deliberately generic: `ShopEasy Store`, EUR as an example currency, English as the default UI language, and UTC as the default time zone. Set the real shop name, currency, time zone, delivery countries, business identity and policies before use. Existing databases keep their saved settings.
