-## Market and brand settings
+Windows users can use [FINALIZE-AND-VERIFY-WINDOWS.ps1](FINALIZE-AND-VERIFY-WINDOWS.ps1). Read [Release verification](RELEASE-VERIFICATION.md) before running either workflow. Do not package `.env`, databases, backups, uploads, private QA artifacts or a virtual environment. The staged deployment prepares and checks a new release before switching `current`; code rollback does not restore database state. Back up and rehearse recovery into a separate empty target.
 
-- Store name: `STORE_NAME`; editable under Manage → Storefront/Branding. The same screen supports an optional dedicated homepage hero image (JPG, PNG or WebP, up to 2 MiB) independent of the first product in the catalogue; the bundled SVG is an illustrative fallback, not product photography.
-- Currency: `STORE_CURRENCY`; choose the actual currency used by the business. Currency may be changed after products or money-based coupons exist, before there is order history. If orders already exist, the selected currency is allowed only when every historical order snapshot already uses that currency; mixed or mismatched histories are blocked because current aggregate reports assume one currency. Historic orders are never converted. Before the first order, affected product prices/costs/sale prices, fixed coupon amounts and monetary coupon minimums are updated to the new currency's minor-unit precision only. This is **not** an exchange-rate conversion. Checkout pauses until a manager enters correct target-market prices and confirms the review. The delivery fee resets to zero and must be configured again.
-- Time zone: `STORE_TIMEZONE`; defaults to UTC. Set an IANA time-zone name such as `Europe/Brussels` or `America/New_York` for the target market.
-- UI language: `DEFAULT_LOCALE=en`, `ckb` (Sorani Kurdish), `ar` (Arabic), or `nl` (Dutch, Belgium). The language does not force a country-specific currency or time zone.
-- Delivery coverage: enter only destinations the seller can fulfil. In addition to the country allow-list, the Manager can configure manual city/postal-prefix delivery-fee overrides and manually entered regional percentage-tax rules. These are seller-supplied calculations, not legal-rate discovery or tax compliance; carrier integration, product-specific tax treatment, filing and jurisdictional certification are not implemented.
+## Capabilities and boundaries
 
-The optional `SEED_DEMO_DATA=true` setting creates illustrative general-retail products in a fresh database. It is off by default. Remove sample data and replace product images, content and prices before customer launch.
+- Manager has full management access; Admin is a restricted read-only overview role. Customer order access requires the authenticated owner or a valid guest bearer (protected cookie or explicit private-code POST field); email plus order number alone is insufficient.
+- One store currency is supported. Precision rescaling before the first order is not exchange-rate conversion. Optional city/postal-prefix delivery-fee overrides and regional percentage-tax rules use values supplied by the operator; these are not legal-rate discovery or tax compliance. There is no statutory-rate lookup, filing or carrier integration.
+- COD is the default. Bank transfers require actual statement review and manual confirmation. Mollie is the only card transaction adapter; PayTabs, FIB, iyzico, ZainCash and Stripe entries are contact/onboarding references. Card details stay on the provider's hosted checkout. Live settlement, refunds, inbox delivery and Peppol acceptance require separate provider/host tests.
+- Privacy tools export data, delete eligible records or explicitly minimize contact data while retaining financial records and references under an operator-selected documented policy. Retained records are pseudonymous; this does not certify legal erasure or anonymity.
+- Automated accessibility checks retain violations and incomplete items. Complete WCAG 2.2 AA, ASVS, physical-device/screen-reader coverage and Windows operation are not established by the bundled tests.
 
-## Important feature limits
+See [Features and limitations](FEATURES-AND-LIMITATIONS.md) for the full scope, [AI integration](AI-INTEGRATION.md) for optional bounded catalogue search, [Third-party notices](THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md) for exact dependency obligations and [Asset provenance](ASSET-PROVENANCE-REGISTER.md) for unresolved asset rights. The local `promise-limit` alias is first-party `@shopeasy/task-limit`, private/UNLICENSED; it is not the external ISC package. The notice inventory has 105 `node_modules` rows: 104 external and one first-party. npm advisory totals may count 106 components because the local vendor workspace is also counted; that is a different inventory, not another cleared third-party package.
 
-- Checkout defaults to **cash on delivery**. The Manager may additionally enable the new **manual bank-transfer** method after entering a valid IBAN or supported local account identifier; bank transfers remain pending until a Manager manually checks the bank statement and confirms the exact amount, currency and unique transaction reference. This is not an automatic bank/API integration. The optional Mollie hosted-card adapter remains the only integrated card provider and stays disabled unless the Manager selects a card-enabled mode, the legal merchant country and currency qualify, a public HTTPS `BASE_URL` exists, and the server has the correct private API key and environment. Production card transactions require `NODE_ENV=production` plus a Mollie `live_` key. A test key cannot activate card checkout by accident; for a non-production staging site only, `MOLLIE_TEST_CHECKOUT_ENABLED=true` explicitly permits a `test_` key. Use test credentials only on a dedicated staging site.
-- The Manager settings include official provider contact/onboarding links for Mollie, PayTabs, FIB, iyzico, ZainCash and Stripe, plus private notes for the store's bank/provider representative. Only Mollie card transactions are implemented in this build; other provider entries are directory/onboarding only, not active integrations. Provider-country lists are not approval guarantees: complete the provider's KYC, confirm payout bank/account requirements and follow local legal rules. Never select a false business country or use a provider to bypass restrictions. Syria is not on Mollie's published merchant-country list; Stripe's policies prohibit dealings linked directly or indirectly to Syria. If merchant eligibility is unresolved, keep COD enabled.
-- ShopEasy never collects or stores card numbers or CVV: card users are redirected to the provider-hosted checkout. Payment state is fetched server-side and validated against the exact order/reference/amount/currency; the webhook is not trusted as proof by itself.
-- Optional order-confirmation and order-status emails are supported through Resend but are **disabled by default**; enable them only after a private test. Idempotency and a daily attempt cap prevent repeat/spam bursts. No carrier tracking integration or manager notification email is included. Password-recovery email is separately configurable.
-- One currency is used for the store. No live exchange rates or customer-specific currency conversion are provided.
-- Delivery uses the configured country allow-list and a default flat fee, with optional manually configured city/postal-prefix fee overrides. Optional regional tax rules use the percentage entered by the seller and block checkout when configured rules do not match the destination. ShopEasy does not look up legal tax rates or implement a complete country tax engine, product exemptions, thresholds, multiple taxes, registrations or filings. Courier booking/tracking is not provided.
-- GDPR/CCPA rights handling and cookie consent are not automatically implemented merely by including policy templates. See the seller-protection checklist and complete the real operational/legal work.
-- A clean test run does not establish security certification, accessibility certification, legal compliance or production readiness. Test with a clean install and real target hosting/database before launch.
